A||||5||mshill||Steering Columns: Manual vs. Auto?||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||10-11-2001||04:28 PM||||Can I take a steering column out of a manual transmission car and put it in an automatic?  I was wondering if there was some lockout of the ignition switch it the car is not in Parl or Nuetral?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero_nightmare||10-11-2001||06:29 PM||||im not sure if you can put the lockout part on a manual tranni coloum or not but i do know you can put a manual coloum on a auto car if you dont mind not having a lock out.<P><P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||1
Z||000002||WaltR||10-11-2001||07:32 PM||||Yes you can. I recently removed the automatic and replaced it with a 5spd. People where telling me I needed a manual column but this is not so. The lockout is not in the column but in the ignition switch attached to the side of it. I dont know if all the swithes are the same, but if not just put the switch from the automatic on the other column and hook up the cable. To use the automatic column with a manual just remove the cable. I am not talking about the part behind the key. the switch is down near the bottom under the dash, it just has a linkage rod from the key.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||10-12-2001||01:10 AM||||Thanks much.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-12-2001||07:35 PM||||The transmission interlock for the automatic works only in park. The interlock acts against the actual switch on top of the column.<P>The manual and automatic columns are very similar besides the interlocks.<P>I believe the ignition switches are the same for both columns. Just that when used in an auto the thing gets the interlock screwed to it.<P>If posible I'd recomend keeping the park interlock in service even with the manual column. It's way too easy to leave the car out of park w/o that interlock. Especially for people used to manual transmissions. There's nothing more embarasing to find your car parked 100feet away from where it was when you left it. There's not much that will make you feel more sick if someone gets hurt while it relocates.<P>There are more notes in my cave about the column and interlock.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||10-13-2001||12:46 PM||||Yeah, it can be done fairly easily. I did it twice, you just have to dissaemble the 2 columns and switch components.||||reg||1
